cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ardentum in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ardentum: quantitative portfolio analysis you can explain"
abstract: >-
  Ardentum is an open-source web platform for building, optimising, simulating and
  backtesting investment portfolios. It combines mean-variance, maximum-Sharpe and
  minimum-CVaR optimisation under explicit constraints (including ESG limits) with
  shrinkage estimators, Black-Litterman views, seeded Monte Carlo simulation,
  walk-forward backtests without look-ahead, and currency-hedged returns, and explains
  the mathematics, assumptions and limitations behind every result. Every calculation
  is tested against closed forms or independent references.
authors:
  - name: "The Ardentum authors"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sgfiscalreview-lab/ardentum"
url: "https://ardentum-frontend.pages.dev"
keywords:
  - portfolio optimisation
  - efficient frontier
  - CVaR
  - Black-Litterman
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - backtesting
  - ESG
  - quantitative finance
  - financial education
